    <string name="settings_money_kinds">Four kinds of money</string>
    <string name="settings_money_usage_title">Pay-as-you-go</string>
    <string name="settings_money_usage_body">Month-to-date spend. When daily numbers exist, they are summed by day.</string>
    <string name="settings_money_prepaid_title">Prepaid balance</string>
    <string name="settings_money_prepaid_body">This month’s burn = balance at month start − current balance. The first month is incomplete without a starting snapshot.</string>
    <string name="settings_money_subscription_title">Subscription</string>
    <string name="settings_money_subscription_body">If the charge day falls in this month, the full amount counts. It is not prorated.</string>
    <string name="settings_money_freetier_title">Free tier</string>
    <string name="settings_money_freetier_body">The total records 0; the quota is shown separately.</string>
    <string name="settings_guide_hero_title">The big number doesn’t include subscriptions</string>
    <string name="settings_guide_hero_body">The largest number on the dashboard is usage, prepaid burn, and overage. Monthly fees like GitHub Copilot sit on their own line and stay out of the breakdown. Read both lines for the full bill.</string>
    <string name="settings_guide_aws_title">Refreshing AWS costs money</string>
    <string name="settings_guide_aws_body">Cost Explorer charges about $0.01 per request. AWS is left out of the global refresh and out of refresh-on-open. For a fresh number, refresh that service yourself — the button shows the price.</string>
    <string name="settings_guide_keys_title">Keys don’t follow you to a new phone</string>
    <string name="settings_guide_keys_body">Keys stay in this device’s Keystore, not in cloud backups. To move phones, use Import and Export in Settings.</string>
    <string name="settings_guide_inbox_title">Services without an API can use the inbox</string>
    <string name="settings_guide_inbox_body">Some services have no public billing API. You can create a reading inbox and report numbers yourself; they still land on the dashboard.</string>
    <string name="settings_guide_widget_title">This month can sit on the Lock Screen</string>
    <string name="settings_guide_widget_body">There are no amount-based push alerts. Put a widget on the Home Screen or Lock Screen and the number is there when you glance. Reminders only ask you to come refresh — they never include an amount.</string>
    <string name="settings_guide_open_hint">Open this usage guide</string>
